From 49a3caca83ac7ac427b0da0bb1a447aa24cac9f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:06:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add an internal module compiler worker request protocol

Serialize finalized CC1 arguments and explicit captured filesystem inputs, using binary snapshot files for main contents and ordered YAML overlays. Unsupported filesystem export is the default and process-local remapped buffers are rejected. The internal clangd worker mode reconstructs the invocation and request view before compiling a staged BMI, and discards failed output.

This foundation is not enabled in ModulesBuilder. The parent must still supervise cancellation and deadlines, terminate and reap the specific child, retain prerequisite read leases, capture the entire filesystem view, and clean up killed-worker outputs and caches. It provides no hard runtime or RSS guarantee by itself.
